  "recommendedHours": 90,
  "description": "Vectors, matrices, linear systems, vector spaces, linear maps, determinants, eigenvalues and analytic geometry, developed as both mathematical theory and computational machinery.",
  "prerequisites": [],
  "outcomes": [
    "Solve linear systems and interpret the structure of their solution sets.",
    "Reason with vector spaces, subspaces, bases, dimension and coordinates.",
    "Represent linear maps by matrices and change between bases.",
    "Use determinants, eigenvalues and eigenvectors to analyze transformations.",
    "Connect algebraic objects to geometric lines, planes, distances and projections."
  ],
